# Firm Rate / Open bid — dedicated agent

This feature has its own branch: `feat/take-it-open-bid`.

**Do not work on:** admin personas, view-as, test-lab, `scripts/setup-admins.ts`, or unrelated Insights/facility work.

## Product names

- **Firm Rate** (`LoadRateMode.TAKE_IT`) — posted pay rate. Carriers book that number only.
- **Allow counters** — Firm Rate only. Carriers may still book the Firm Rate instantly, or submit a counter the mill accepts/declines.
- **Open bid** (`LoadRateMode.OPEN_BID`) — no instant book. Carriers bid until the mill accepts or `bidWindowExpiresAt`.

## Behavior

- Book API must use the posted Firm Rate (ignore client-typed rates). Reject Open bid books; tell them to bid.
- One pending bid/counter per carrier per load (update in place). Adjusting a bid resets the 24h supplier accept clock.
- Accepting a bid books the load at that amount and declines other pending bids.
- Open bid window hard max **72h**. Same load id: max **2** bid cycles; cycle 2 end without accept → `UNLISTED`.
- Firm Rate stays on the board **7 days** past pickup (vs 48h for Open bid). After that → `NEEDS_REPOST` + in-app alert (email stub PENDING). Soft-warn on new post; do not hard-block.
- Bids and posted rates must sit inside the lane stop-gaps (default ±30% of the rolling average; ±50% on thin lanes). No band until there is at least one comparable lumber move.
- Decision context on book/bid (avg, last book on the lane, $/mi, allowed range) is free. Full Insights stays a future monthly add-on.
- Open Bids nav shows a pending inbox count (mill: bids to review; carrier: bids waiting on the mill).
- Facility/driver pages must never show rates.
- Posted-lane analytics: `LaneRateObservation` with `source=POSTED`, `outcome`, optional `bookedRateUsd` — separate from booked freight market views.

